WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.830
Rarely is it as emotional and heartwarming
to talk about a fictional character as is

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:18.300
the case with Donxiquote Rosinante. Despite
his very short appearance in the story, as

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.770
well as a complete lack of interaction with
any of the main protagonists, Corazon, as

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:29.070
he was known within the Doflamingo family,
is one of the most beloved characters in the

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:36.010
entire story. How come then, that a side character
with no badass devil fruit powers, no advanced

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:42.030
Haki and - due to his early death - no active
impact on the current story line, has become

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:48.300
such a fan-favourite that is almost as iconic
for the story of one piece, as his older brother

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:55.559
Doflamingo, the main antagonist of the longest
story arc until Wano? In this video, we will

00:00:55.559 --> 00:01:02.010
not only answer this question, but explore
in depth why Corazon is actually one of the

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:08.220
best-written characters in the entire story.
Oh, yeah and if you haven’t done so already,

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:13.830
make sure to subscribe to the channel. It’s
free and you get updates on any of my future

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:21.720
videos.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:27.560
The secret behind Oda’s success with Corazon’s
character lies in his interaction with two

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.320
other, by the time of his first appearance
already strongly established characters in

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:38.430
the story. We have known Doflamingo from way
before the time skip with Oda revealing more

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:44.840
and more of his narcissistic and tyrannical
nature over time as we approach Dressrosa.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.490
And while it’s true that we didn’t get
to meet Law until we reached Sabaody, he has

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:55.310
been present in almost every single arc since
his first introduction, interacting and traveling

00:01:55.310 --> 00:02:02.220
with the crew. Between these two characters,
Oda has established Corazon as the missing

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:08.420
puzzle piece to link both Law and Dofi, and
has used Corazon’s relationship with both

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:13.891
to give deep-reaching characterisation to
his character in a very short time, through

00:02:13.891 --> 00:02:20.650
both Doflamingo’s and Law’s respective
flashbacks. So, let’s look at both of these

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:30.280
relationships in a bit more detail.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:35.690
Just as his older brother Dofi, Rosinante
was born into the ranks of the celestial dragons,

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:41.730
but left Marijoe very early on in his life
to live among the commoners with his family.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:46.730
While right from the start Doflamingo was
shown to be engulfed in feelings of superiority

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:54.480
and anger, Rosinante was quite the opposite.
Even as a child he was a very sensitive and

00:02:54.480 --> 00:03:02.041
kind boy, that in direct contrast to his brother
expressed a deep love for his family. When

00:03:02.041 --> 00:03:06.730
their father’s decision ultimately lead
to the doom of their family, Doflamingo felt

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:12.800
nothing but rage and hatred for everyone involved,
which resulted in him executing his father

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:19.060
Homing while he was holding the young Rosinante,
who had reacted to their tragic circumstances

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:25.790
with sadness and an even stronger emotional
connection to his family. Seeing his brother

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.950
spiral into deeper and deeper darkness, and
witnessing him murdering their father while

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:37.230
being embraced in his arms deeply traumatised
him. And so while Dofi was busy bringing their

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:41.980
fathers head back to the celestial dragons
and started gathering power-hungry people

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:48.400
around him, Rosinante was found by none other
than the future fleet admiral Sengoku, who

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:58.519
took him into the Marines and raised him.

00:03:58.519 --> 00:04:04.950
From very early on, Corazon knew that Doflamingo’s
cruelty &amp; tyranny was not caused by the tragic

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:10.659
events surrounding their family, but merely
amplified by them. Thus, both brothers are

00:04:10.659 --> 00:04:17.440
the perfect example of nature vs nurture.
Despite growing up the exact same way and

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:23.660
experiencing the exact same pain, both of
them turned out to be as different as one

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:29.960
could imagine. Nonetheless, despite their
polar personalities. both brothers still felt

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:35.729
connected in some strange sense. Rosinante
felt responsible for reigning in his brothers

00:04:35.729 --> 00:04:41.760
actions and thus returned back to his side
as a Marine spy fourteen years later. When

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:48.160
he ultimately was on the run with Law, his
true identity was revealed to Dofi. Both brothers

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:54.250
were evidently not eager to go against each
other. But while Corazon was ultimately unable

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:59.860
to shoot his brother, Doflamingo, although
clearly troubled, didn’t hesitate to shoot

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:05.750
his little brother, once again putting himself
above everyone else, as he had done his entire

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:13.590
life.

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:20.130
The point of all this, is that through Dofi
Corazon is characterised as his polar opposite.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:26.710
Two strikingly different paths, based on the
same starting point. Thus, in stark contrast

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:31.620
to his brother, we get too know Corazon as
someone who is able to feel and express real

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:39.159
emotions and who has a strong sense of compassion
and altruism. Thus, the major difference between

00:05:39.159 --> 00:06:29.870
Doflamingo and Rosinante that I think Oda
tried to drive home, is the concept of self-sacrifice.

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:40.150
A 

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:45.460
parent-figure sacrificing themselves for a
beloved child is a consistent theme throughout

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:52.349
One Piece. While Doflamingo's character carries
his own tragedy in many ways, as I thoroughly

00:06:52.349 --> 00:06:58.440
discuss in his video, the major difference
between him and his brother is that to Dofi,&nbsp;no

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:05.479
one&nbsp;will ever be as important as himself.
He might care for others to a certain extent

00:07:05.479 --> 00:07:11.000
as long as they are useful and loyal to him,
but ultimately, he will always choose what's

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:18.259
best for himself - Dofi First. Rosinante was
just as traumatised as Doflamingo in his own

00:07:18.259 --> 00:07:25.340
way. And yet he chose to act on those feelings
in a completely opposite way. Instead of choosing

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:32.270
to make himself and his own ambitions a priority,
dedicating his life to protecting others from

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:42.300
experiencing the same kinds of pain and trauma
he lived through as 

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.850
a child.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:50.650
As a result, next to relying general intel
back to the Marines, Corazon’s main goal

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:55.509
was to keep Doflamingo from recruiting more
and more children into his ranks, including

00:07:55.509 --> 00:08:03.960
the likes of Dellinger, Baby 5 , Buffalo and
of course - the young Trafalgar Law. Law’s

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:09.159
relationship with Corazon might well be the
most well-written in the entire story outside

00:08:09.159 --> 00:08:15.229
of the main straw hat crew. The level of passion
and thought that Oda evidently poured into

00:08:15.229 --> 00:08:21.599
these two characters and their time together,
to me is clear proof of how important Law

00:08:21.599 --> 00:08:27.210
has become to Oda himself and to the story.
And while he isn’t an official straw hat,

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:33.770
he certainly has received a flashback and
tragic backstory worthy of one.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:38.870
How this relationship formed and how Oda chives
this incredibly powerful sentiment throughout

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:46.130
the flashback, in my opinion deserves its
own video. Thus we will explore this in a

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:51.769
thorough scene analysis. What we should take
away for Rosinante’s character here however,

00:08:51.769 --> 00:08:56.600
is that right from the start he cared for
Law and wanted to ultimately free him from

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:02.910
Doflamingo’s grasp as soon as possible.
However, over time, Corazon’s motive shifted

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:08.250
away from doing everything in his power to
stop his brother’s tyranny, to doing everything

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:15.070
in his power heal Law’s sickness, protecting
him from Dofi and giving him a real shot at

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:23.589
a happier life.

00:09:23.589 --> 00:09:30.839
And I think it was exactly this decision,
to chose Law over both his real family Doflamingo

00:09:30.839 --> 00:09:38.220
and his duties within the Marines, that truly
made his character so powerful and likeable.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:43.120
Not only did he give the traumatised Law a
sense of hope again, but he also gave him

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:50.779
unconditional and genuine love and care. This
way he was not only able to heal Law’s body,

00:09:50.779 --> 00:09:56.950
but also his heart, and so put him on the
right track to live a good life and keep him

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:03.420
from becoming the next Doflamingo. Due to
his own childhood, he was able to look past

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:09.899
Law's deep-rooted anger and hatred and see
the suffering that caused them. And so, while

00:10:09.899 --> 00:10:15.480
Dofi was willing to give Law what he&nbsp;wanted&nbsp;-
the opportunity to inflict his own pain onto

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:21.230
others until his inevitable death due to his
sickness - Corazon was able to give Law what

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:27.910
he&nbsp;actually needed: A chance to heal enough
to live a good life and leave behind all his

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:36.560
pain and sorrow.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:42.269
I think the best way to truly understand the
essence of Rosinante’s character, is through

00:10:42.269 --> 00:10:48.850
the symbolism that Oda has integrated in his
character. Corazon unites a number of central

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:53.470
themes and symbols in One Piece, that we have
already discussed in detail throughout this

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:59.310
series of videos. For example the concept
of dreams, as he is fully convinced that he

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:06.870
will find a way to save Law, something seemingly
impossible. The concept of inherited Will,

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:12.959
as he pushes Law to find the truth about the
will of D and his heritage. And the concept

00:11:12.959 --> 00:11:19.350
of immortality according to Dr. Hiruluk, that
people only die when they and their dreams

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:25.820
are forgotten. By showing true love to Law,
he managed to gain the immortality, that his

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:29.000
brother was yearning for so badly.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:33.949
All of this is wonderfully reflected in the
main theme of Rosinante’s character - the

00:11:33.949 --> 00:11:40.880
heart - which goes far beyond his choice of
fashion. Corazon, which means heart in Spanish,

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:48.829
is what Dofi wanted from Law. Consume the
heart-shaped Op-Op no Mi and give him immortality.

00:11:48.829 --> 00:11:53.910
But I think most importantly, Corazon was
able to heal Law’s own heart through his

00:11:53.910 --> 00:12:00.269
love and kindness, which is why ultimately
Law became captain of the heart pirates, in

00:12:00.269 --> 00:12:06.740
memory of his father-figure. In the end, while
Doflamingo themed his crew around the concept

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:14.000
of a family, Law’s and Corazon’s relationship
was way more real a family than Dofi’s could

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:20.130
ever have Benn. And so, to answer the question
once and for all. The reason why Donquixote

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:27.310
Rosinante is such a fantastic and beloved
character, is the immense sense of love and

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:33.920
kindness that Oda was able to portray through
his character. A character written so well,

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:39.490
that his pure &amp; selfless actions couldn’t
help but transcend the story itself and touch

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:51.910
the hearts of its readers. If you want to
dive even deeper into this, you can watch

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:57.769
my entire analysis of Doflamingo on the top,
and the analysis of Corazon’s and Law’s

00:12:57.769 --> 00:13:00.720
backstory below. Thanks guys. Peace.

